text: "---\nmodule: \"05-POST-DELIVERY\"\npart: \"A\"\ntitle: \"Testimonials & Reviews\"\nversion: \"2026.05\"\nstatus: \"Production-Ready\"\n---\n\n# 05A: Testimonials & Reviews\n\n> **Core Principle:** A testimonial from a satisfied client is worth more than 100 cold emails. It is social proof that converts prospects into buyers.\n>\n> *\"Asking for a video testimonial: 'Hey XYZ, it would be really awesome and helpful for us if you could just record a 1-2min honest video testimonial about our service and if you'd like to recommend us to others?'\"* — Him Singh\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [The 3-Ask Testimonial Method](#1-the-3-ask-testimonial-method)\n2. [Testimonial Formats](#2-testimonial-formats)\n3. [Collection Scripts](#3-collection-scripts)\n4. [Display Strategy](#4-display-strategy)\n5. [Review Generation](#5-review-generation)\n6. [AI Prompts](#6-ai-prompts)\n7. [Action Checklist](#7-action-checklist)\n\n---\n\n## 1. The 3-Ask Testimonial Method\n\n### The Timeline\n\n| Ask | Timing | Method | Expected Yes Rate | Purpose |\n|-----|--------|--------|-------------------|---------|\n| **Ask 1** | At delivery (within 48 hours) | In-person or video call | 60-70% | Capture enthusiasm while fresh |\n| **Ask 2** | At 30 days | Email with metrics | 50-60% | Validate long-term results |\n| **Ask 3** | At 90 days | Email + LinkedIn | 30-40% | Request referral intro |\n\n### Why the 3-Ask Works\n\n1. **At delivery:** Client is excited, project is fresh, emotions are high\n2. **At 30 days:** Client has seen results, can speak to impact\n3. **At 90 days:** Client trusts you, knows your work, willing to vouch\n\n### The Escalation of Ask\n\n```\nAsk 1 (Delivery): \"Quick testimonial?\" → Low friction\nAsk 2 (30 days): \"Case study feature?\" → Medium commitment\nAsk 3 (90 days): \"Referral intro?\" → High trust required\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Testimonial Formats\n\n### Format 1: Video Testimonial (Most Powerful)\n\n**Specifications:**\n| Attribute | Specification |\n|-----------|--------------|\n| Length | 1-2 minutes |\n| Quality | Phone camera acceptable, good lighting |\n| Setting | Client's office or natural environment |\n| Questions | 4 scripted prompts |\n| Editing | Minimal (trim start/end, add logo) |\n\n**The 4 Questions to Ask:**\n1. \"What problem were you facing before working with us?\"\n2. \"What did we build/solve for you?\"\n3. \"What specific result did you achieve? (with numbers if possible)\"\n4. \"Would you recommend us to others?\"\n\n**Recording Tips:**\n- Send questions 24 hours in advance\n- Offer to record via Zoom (you control the file)\n- Provide Loom link as easy alternative\n- Give them 3 takes (no pressure)\n\n### Format 2: Written Testimonial\n\n**Template for Client:**\n```\n\"Before working with [Your Name], we were struggling with [specific pain].\n\nThey built [specific solution] which [specific outcome].\n\nThe result: [quantified metric].\n\nI would highly recommend [Your Name] to any [target client] looking \nto [specific outcome].\"\n```\n\n**Where to Use:**\n- Website homepage\n- Proposal appendices\n- LinkedIn recommendations\n- Upwork/Contra reviews\n- Email signatures\n\n### Format 3: Case Study (Most Detailed)\n\n**Structure:** STAR-M (Situation, Task, Action, Result, Metrics)\n\nSee Module 01C for full case study template.\n\n### Format 4: Social Proof Screenshot\n\n**What to Screenshot:**\n- Slack/Teams praise messages\n- Email thank-you notes\n- LinkedIn endorsements\n- Payment confirmations with nice notes\n- Post-project survey responses\n\n**Where to Post:**\n- LinkedIn carousel\n- Instagram stories\n- Twitter/X threads\n- Website social proof section\n\n---\n\n## 3. Collection Scripts\n\n### Script 1: At Delivery (Video)\n\n```\n\"Hey [Name], I'm so glad we got this across the finish line!\n\nWould you do me a quick favor? I'm building my portfolio and \nwould love a 1-2 minute video from you about the project.\n\nNothing fancy — just your phone camera, good light, and honest \nthoughts on:\n1. What problem you had\n2. What we built\n3. What result you got\n\nI can send you the questions in advance, or we can hop on a \nquick Zoom and I'll record it for you. Whatever's easier.\n\nNo pressure at all — just thought I'd ask while the project's \nfresh in your mind!\n\nThanks,\n[Your name]\"\n```\n\n### Script 2: At 30 Days (Written + Metrics)\n\n```\nSubject: Quick check-in + favor?\n\nHi [Name],\n\nHope [system/project] is running smoothly! It's been 30 days \nsince launch.\n\nQuick questions:\n1. How are the metrics looking? Any wins you've noticed?\n2. Is the team finding it useful?\n3. Any tweaks or questions?\n\nAlso — if you're happy with the results, would you mind writing \na brief testimonial? Just 2-3 sentences about your experience.\n\nEven better: if you have any metrics you can share (anonymized \nis fine), I'd love to feature your success in a case study.\n\nEither way, happy to jump on a quick call if helpful.\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\"\n```\n\n### Script 3: At 90 Days (Referral)\n\n```\nSubject: Who else should know about this?\n\nHi [Name],\n\nIt's been 3 months since we launched [project], and I hope \nit's still delivering value for [Company].\n\nQuick ask: do you know anyone in your network who might be \nfacing similar [pain point] challenges?\n\nI'm looking for 2-3 more [type of company] to work with this \nquarter, and a warm intro from you would mean the world.\n\nAs a thank you, I'll [incentive: $500 credit, free month of \nsupport, free audit, etc.] for any referral that becomes a client.\n\nNo worries at all if no one comes to mind — just thought I'd ask!\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Display Strategy\n\n### The Testimonial Portfolio\n\n| Location | Format | Purpose |\n|----------|--------|---------|\n| **Website homepage** | 3 video testimonials above fold | Immediate trust |\n| **Services page** | Relevant testimonial per service | Contextual proof |\n| **Case studies** | Embedded quote + video | Deep credibility |\n| **LinkedIn Featured** | Screenshot + link | Profile trust |\n| **Proposals** | 1 relevant testimonial | Close deals |\n| **Email signature** | Rotating quote | Passive proof |\n| **Upwork/Contra** | 5-star reviews | Platform ranking |\n\n### The Testimonial Wall\n\nCreate a dedicated page on your website:\n\n```\n# What Clients Say\n\n[Video 1: Client A — 90 sec]\n\"Reduced churn by 34% in 90 days\"\n— [Name], [Title], [Company]\n\n[Video 2: Client B — 60 sec]\n\"Best investment we made this year\"\n— [Name], [Title], [Company]\n\n[Written 1: Client C]\n\"[Quote]\"\n— [Name], [Title], [Company]\n\n[Written 2: Client D]\n\"[Quote]\"\n— [Name], [Title], [Company]\n\n[Case Study Link: Client E]\n\"Full case study: How we saved $24K/year\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Review Generation\n\n### Platform Review Strategy\n\n| Platform | When to Ask | How to Ask | Impact |\n|----------|-------------|------------|--------|\n| **Upwork** | At project close | \"Mind leaving a quick review?\" | JSS score, visibility |\n| **Contra** | At project close | \"Would love your feedback on Contra\" | Profile ranking |\n| **LinkedIn** | Anytime | \"Would you write me a recommendation?\" | Profile credibility |\n| **Google** | After 30 days | \"Would you leave a Google review?\" | Local SEO |\n| **Clutch** | Enterprise clients | \"Would you submit a review on Clutch?\" | B2B credibility |\n| **G2** | SaaS/tool projects | \"Would you review us on G2?\" | Product credibility |\n\n### The Review Request Email\n\n```\nSubject: Quick favor — 2 minutes?\n\nHi [Name],\n\nWorking with you on [project] was a highlight of my quarter.\n\nIf you have 2 minutes, would you leave a review on [platform]? \nIt really helps other [target clients] find me.\n\n[Direct link to review page]\n\nNo pressure at all — just thought I'd ask!\n\nThanks,\n[Your name]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. AI Prompts\n\n### Prompt 1: Testimonial Request Writer\n\n```\nAct as a client success manager.\n\nClient details:\n- Name: [NAME]\n- Company: [COMPANY]\n- Project: [WHAT YOU BUILT]\n- Result: [QUANTIFIED OUTCOME]\n- Days since delivery: [X]\n\nWrite 3 testimonial request messages:\n1. Day-of-delivery request (casual, immediate)\n2. 30-day check-in (metrics-focused, case study angle)\n3. 90-day referral ask (warm intro request)\n\nEach must:\n- Reference specific project details\n- Make it easy to say yes (low friction)\n- Include an incentive or thank-you\n- Sound personal, not templated\n```\n\n### Prompt 2: Testimonial Editor\n\n```\nAct as a copy editor for client testimonials.\n\nRaw testimonial:\n\"[PASTE RAW TESTIMONIAL]\"\n\nEdit to:\n1. Lead with the problem (first 10 words)\n2. Include specific outcome (with numbers)\n3. End with recommendation\n4. Keep under 50 words\n5. Maintain client's voice and authenticity\n\nProvide 3 versions:\n- Short (25 words)\n- Medium (40 words)\n- Long (75 words)\n```\n\n### Prompt 3: Case Study from Testimonial\n\n```\nAct as a case study writer.\n\nTestimonial content:\n\"[PASTE TESTIMONIAL]\"\n\nProject details:\n- Client: [COMPANY]\n- Industry: [INDUSTRY]\n- Duration: [WEEKS]\n- Tech stack: [TOOLS]\n\nExpand into a mini case study (300 words):\n1. Situation (2 sentences)\n2. Task (1 sentence)\n3. Action (2-3 bullets)\n4. Result (with metrics)\n5. Quote (from testimonial)\n\nMake it ready for website publication.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Action Checklist\n\n### At Delivery (Within 48 Hours)\n\n- [ ] Send testimonial request (video preferred)\n- [ ] Send Upwork/Contra review request (if applicable)\n- [ ] Screenshot any praise from Slack/email\n- [ ] Add project to portfolio\n- [ ] Schedule 30-day check-in\n\n### At 30 Days\n\n- [ ] Send check-in email with metrics request\n- [ ] Ask for written testimonial\n- [ ] Ask for case study participation\n- [ ] Request LinkedIn recommendation\n- [ ] Update case study with results\n\n### At 90 Days\n\n- [ ] Send referral request\n- [ ] Ask for introduction to 2-3 contacts\n- [ ] Offer referral incentive\n- [ ] Update website with new testimonial\n- [ ] Share testimonial on social media\n\n### Ongoing\n\n- [ ] Maintain testimonial tracker (who, when, format, status)\n- [ ] Rotate testimonials on website quarterly\n- [ ] Add testimonials to proposals\n- [ ] Request 1 new testimonial per month\n\n---\n\n> **Next:** [05B: Maintenance & Retainers →](05B-MAINTAINERS-RETAINERS.md)\n>\n> *\"A testimonial is a gift that keeps on giving. Ask for it, display it, profit from it.\"*\n\n---\n\n*Module 05A | Testimonials & Reviews | Version 2026.05*\n"
